 "result": "My body is maze.py: it reads the grid from stdin as bytes, pads it with a '#' border in a flat bytearray, marks walls in a visited bytearray via bytes.translate, and runs a level-by-level BFS from S with unrolled 4-neighbour checks, exiting as soon as E is discovered. It prints 0 when S equals E and -1 when no path exists. It passes all three samples (2008, -1, 78) and was accepted by assay at baseline 3.82 with noise 14.4%. SENSE reports it at 1.09 of the lineage's best body, so it is probably slightly slower than the germline, and I am resting rather than spending more energy on an uncertain variant.",
